                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wish I could neutral rate this game rather than either \"good\" or \"bad\"\r\n\r\nThere's a lot I dislike about this game. The map isn't very helpful. You spend most of your time running from one side of the school to the other just to realize that you missed out on your time window and have to wait a full cycle. There's so much in this game that's unnecessarily tedious. You have to go through every single dungeon again at the end of the game and fight all their bosses again. The mines map is just waiting for a long time and hoping you guess the right path. The Ice Dragon fight takes way too long to be able to hit. I have absolutely no idea how I beat the final boss when it goes into it's \"invincible phase\". \r\n\r\nHowever despite all that I love LWA and liked seeing another little adventure with these characters. The story was pretty cute and the cutscenes look like they come straight from the anime. When your life isn't being ruined by horrible dungeon design, the gameplay is actually pretty solid. As bad as the map was, I did like exploring the school and seeing everything it had to offer, and there's a lot of sidequests so if you don't want to spend an hour fighting an ice dragon you can just do something else. \r\n\r\nSo should you get this game? Ask yourself these 2 questions:\r\nDo you love LWA?\r\nIs the game on sale?\r\nIf you answered \"yes\" to both of these, then maybe it wouldn't be a bad idea if you wanted more from the series. Otherwise, I'd skip out on this.",
